{"chunk_id": "1d863425f304", "text": "In the Mahaprasthanika Parva, the final earthly journey of the Pandavas begins after the destruction of the Yadavas and Krishna\u2019s departure. Realizing the dominance of Time and the end of their era, Yudhishthira installs Parikshit as king and renounces the world with his brothers and Draupadi. Clad in bark garments, they set out on a great pilgrimage across the earth toward the Himalayas, followed by a mysterious dog. Along the ascent toward Meru, each companion falls due to a subtle moral flaw\u2014Draupadi\u2019s partiality, Sahadeva\u2019s pride in wisdom, Nakula\u2019s pride in beauty, Arjuna\u2019s boastfulness, and Bhima\u2019s gluttony and vanity. Yudhishthira alone continues without looking back. When Indra invites him to heaven, he refuses to abandon the faithful dog, revealing his unwavering commitment to dharma. The dog proves to be Dharma himself, confirming Yudhishthira\u2019s righteousness as he ascends to heaven in his human body.\nThe Pandavas renounce their kingdom, journey north toward heaven, companions fall for hidden flaws, and Yudhishthira proves supreme righteousness by refusing to abandon a loyal dog.\nThemes: renunciation, moral judgment of flaws, loyalty and compassion, end of heroic age, dharma tested", "vector": [0.02287217043340206, -0.028235578909516335, -0.01906239427626133, -0.00500539829954505, -0.017427701503038406, 0.03993510454893112, -0.0157119520008564, -0.01615777611732483, -0.014833811670541763, -0.010098610073328018, 0.010071590542793274, 0.017684388905763626, 0.013232894241809845, 0.012030518613755703, -0.010139139369130135, 6.41189981251955e-05, 0.04877054691314697, -0.01661711186170578, 0.02993782050907612, 0.005130364093929529, -0.014806792140007019, -0.020507946610450745, -0.005616718903183937, -0.0008561864960938692, 0.0017081511905416846, 0.02227773703634739, 0.030640332028269768, -0.017805976793169975, 0.0015004373854026198, -0.00012232744484208524, -0.012010253965854645, 0.0